# Invalid config: a VRRP group whose virtual-address leaf-list violates
# min-elements 1, in both spellings.
#
# VALIDATES: YANG min-elements enforcement for a leaf-list, driven through
# `ze config validate` -- the operator-facing path -- rather than a unit test.
# PREVENTS: min-elements silently enforcing nothing. It did exactly that until
# 2026-07-20: walkTree guarded its cardinality call with `if len(items) > 0`, so
# zero -- the ONE count that violates a minimum -- was the one count that skipped
# the check, and absence was not scanned at all. max-elements was unaffected (an
# over-count is necessarily non-empty), which is why the sibling
# sysctl-profile-max-elements.ci passed throughout while this bound did nothing.
#
# Two cases on purpose, because they took different code paths to fix:
#   seq=1  virtual-address OMITTED  -- the shape an operator actually writes.
#          Nothing caught this before: goyang never sets Mandatory on a leaf-list
#          (its *LeafList node has no mandatory field), so walkTree's mandatory
#          loop can never fire on one.
#   seq=2  virtual-address [ ]      -- explicitly empty.
#
# Both also draw a second error from the VRRP plugin verifier, which owns the same
# leaf-list. That duplicate is accepted deliberately (spec R-7): suppressing the
# YANG one would need a registry of which plugin owns which leaf-list, i.e. exactly
# the per-feature spelling in a generic package that plugin-self-containment
# forbids. So this test asserts on the YANG diagnostic specifically.
option=skip-os:value=darwin

stdin=absent:terminator=EOF_ABSENT
interface {
    backend netlink;
    ethernet eth0 {
        unit 0 {
            ipv4 {
                address [ 192.0.2.251/24 ];
                vrrp {
                    group uplink {
                        vrid 10;
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
EOF_ABSENT

stdin=empty:terminator=EOF_EMPTY
interface {
    backend netlink;
    ethernet eth0 {
        unit 0 {
            ipv4 {
                address [ 192.0.2.251/24 ];
                vrrp {
                    group uplink {
                        vrid 10;
                        virtual-address [ ];
                    }
                }
            }
        }
    }
}
EOF_EMPTY

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=absent:exit=1
cmd=foreground:seq=2:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=empty:exit=1
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=too few entries: 0 (minimum 1)
expect=stdout:contains=virtual-address
